## VERDICT
**ALREADY_FIXED** (path-A dual refuse). No product source change this turn.

Stmt `println` is still special-cased (`c_emit_ident_stmt` → `c_emit_println`)
and **does not** call `c_secret_emit_guard` / `c_guard_scan_idents`. That
skip is the s71_security R1 / SPRINT 2.9 “unify later” sentence — **not**
a SECRET fail-open.

Path-A contract (fail-closed SECRET IDENT at product `println`/`eprintln`,
string-lit no-FP, alias `let f = println; f(SECRET)`) already holds on
**three** front doors:

| Door | Who refuses |
|------|-------------|
| `oodac check` | `check_secret_println_sinks` IDENT walk + `c_secret_refuse_sink_resolved` |
| `oodac emit-c` | **same** walk first (`c_emit.oo` L86, then `process_exit`) |
| `oodac emit-llvm` | **same** walk first (`llvm_emit.oo` L79) |

`eprintln` / `let f = println; f(...)` already hit `c_secret_emit_guard`
**after** that front door (free-call lower). Routing stmt `println`
through the C-text guard would be I5 theater (fake joined `args` on a
multi-`oo_print_*` builtin) with **no new refuse**. Check cannot call
the guard (wrong signature: C texts, not toks) — that is the false
DE2.9 sentence.

Monofiles: `c_emit_print.oo` **87**, `c_emit_ident.oo` **228**,
`c_emit_secret_guard.oo` **228**, `c_emit_secret.oo` **264** (all ≤600).

